  "worked_solution": "First, we find the value of the function at $R$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3,2) & =20-(3)^{2}-2(2)^{2}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the level curve that passes through $R(3,2)$ is the $3$-level curve.\n\nRecall that the level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=3.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ 20-{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2} & =3 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2{y}^{2} & =17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level curve that passes through $R(3,2)$ is the ellipse ${x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}=17.$",
